<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45269" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stătĭcŭlum</span></b> ,
			i, n.
		statua. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A little statue</i> or <i>image</i>,
				<i>a statuette</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34,
				17, 48, § 163</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 10, 54, §
			140</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Of <i>images of the gods</i>, <i>idols</i>, as a transl. of the Heb. ,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Gnost. 2</span></i> ex Deut.
			12, 3; <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i> ex Lev. 26, 1.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
